      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FOR SALE HOUSE\r\nAT KNOCKASKEHEEN, \r\nLISDOONVARNA, CO. CLARE V95 K5W4\r\nFOR SALE BY PRIVATE TREATY. \r\n\r\nCOTTAGE ON CIRCA 0.74 ACRES   \r\n\r\nCompany license number 003178\r\nVIEWING STRICTLY BY ADVANCED APPOINTMENT WITH SOLE AGENT STREETS AHEAD PROPERTIES\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION:\r\nStreets Ahead Properties are delighted to bring to the market this traditional detached two storey farmhouse with outbuildings, built more than 100 years ago, sitting on circa 0.74 acres and contained in Folio CE10861.  \r\n\r\nThe property is located on the main R477 just 2.5km from Lisdoonvarna a small spa town in north County Clare on Ireland’s west coast, located near the spectacular Cliffs of Moher and the unique limestone landscape of The Burren. The town is famous for its mineral-rich spring waters, which led to its development as a Victorian spa destination in the 19th century. Today, \r\nLisdoonvarna is best known for hosting the annual Lisdoonvarna Matchmaking Festival, one of Ireland’s oldest and most famous festivals, attracting thousands of visitors from around the world each year. With its traditional Irish music, welcoming atmosphere, and scenic surroundings, Lisdoonvarna remains an important cultural and tourism centre in County Clare.\r\nDoolin is within a 10-minute drive - Doolin has always been designated as one of Ireland's most popular tourist destinations and in 2019, was awarded Failte Irelands destination award. Doolin is widely regarded as The Home of Traditional Irish Music but also for its warm welcome, food and its close proximity to The Aran Islands, The famous Cliffs of Moher, Doolin Cave and the unique Burren Landscape.\r\n\r\nThe house is comprised of 5 bedrooms, 1 bathroom, living room, kitchen/ dining room.  Heating is by way of a range in the kitchen, heating radiators throughout. There are UPVC windows and doors under a slate roof.  The property would be in  need of major renovations to bring it up to modern days standards, however structurally the property is well built on an elevated site with extensive views of the surrounding countryside.  There are opportunities to renovate and upgrade all the various sheds and outhouses attached to the property.  \r\nCurrent government grants would be available with this property.\r\n\r\nBER: G\r\nYEAR OF CONSTRUCTION:  1960\r\nAPPROXIMATE FLOOR AREA: 128.32SqM\r\n\r\nAn early viewing is highly recommended Viewings strictly by advance appointment with sole agent Streets Ahead Properties. \r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION – APPROXIMATE DIMENSIONS:\r\nFront Porch: (3.05m x 2.28m) Tiled floor, large PVC windows and door.\r\n\r\nHallway: (1.22m x 1.52m) Leading into the main house,  staircase leading to the first floor.\r\n\r\nLiving Area: (4.33m x 3.68m) Front aspect, Laminate timber floor, Aga solid fuel stove, hot-press and fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining: (5.52m x 5.30m)  Oil fired stove heating radiators, eye level and base units, linoleum floor, door to rear garden.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1/Sitting Room: (3.30m x 4.07m) Front and side aspect.\r\n\r\nLobby: (1.17 x 1.06) \r\n\r\nBathroom: (3.09m x 1.32m) Partially tiled, walk in shower, whb and wc.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: (3.93m x 2.47m) Side aspect, linoleum floor, radiator.\r\n\r\nLanding: (5.03m x 1.17m) Carpet floor, radiator.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3: (4.87m x 3.33m) Front aspect, carpet floor, radiator.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4: (3.34m x 1.66m) + (1.12m x 1.35m) L shaped room with front aspect and linoleum floor, radiator.\r\n\r\nBedroom 5: (3.34m x 2.27m) Front aspect, carpet floor, radiator.\r\n\r\n\r\nEXTERNAL:\r\n\r\n Shed:  (18m x 5m) For storage of fuel and gardening tools.\r\n\r\n\r\nDisclaimer\r\nNote: Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs are provided for guidance purposes only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Only 4 mins from Lisdoonvarna and 7 mins from Doolin.\r\nPivotal to North Clare towns, villages and beaches - Doolin, Ennistymon, Lahinch and Liscannor.\r\nGreat starter home or Investment opportunity.\r\n5-bedroom, two storey farmhouse on 0.74 aces.\r\nOutbuildings attached."
      },
